{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/912094-pantheon-creation-with-the-titans-helping","id":912094,"title":"Pantheon Creation With the Titans Helping","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-10T22:12:54-07:00","id":912094,"title":"Pantheon Creation With the Titans Helping","content":"I Just came up with this really cool idea, We kniw for a fact Scions can create new pantheons,althought there's no mechanics in how to do it just yet,i was thinking that almost all ancinet pantheons had their start with the Titans,the first gods were issues of the titans. I realized,if a band of scions like the sample characters from the first edition were to create a new pantheon,could they strike a deal with the titans to help? (i know <i>all </i>titans were evil in the first edition,but bear with me here). My idea is that the Band could convince a titan to make a connection with their brand new pantheon,one of more mebers of the band would somehow bond with a avatar of titans and they would be connected forever. And they would throw away their relationships with their divine parents and instead be reborn as &quot;scions&quot; of titans. But not like a corrupted scion,they would become flesh and blood of titans,just like any son or daughter of titans would be. so,the same way zeus poseidon and hades and their sisters founded the theoi after being born of cronos and rhea,a modern scion could crteate a new pantheon with the titans help","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 06-11-2016, 01:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T23:23:47-07:00","id":912117,"title":"","content":"Yes, but I don't see why they would even need the Titans help, unless they convert a few into gods to pad out their Pantheon. After all Zeus and Friends founded their pantheon in conquering the Titans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T23:37:29-07:00","id":912121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/912094-pantheon-creation-with-the-titans-helping?p=912117#post912117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but I don't see why they would even need the Titans help, unless they convert a few into gods to pad out their Pantheon. After all Zeus and Friends founded their pantheon in conquering the Titans.</div> </div> </div> </div>i thought acutally be allied to titan or more could give the new panthoen an edge agains those who saw all titans as enemies","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T23:54:59-07:00","id":912128,"title":"","content":"The 'All Titans are EVIL' issue of 1st edition was sort of a hard pill to swallow. It made things easier in the sence that they were simpler. Gods good...titans bad...smash titans. But there are so many stories about gods getting along with titans, falling for them and having children with them and working along side them that you have to ignore a lot of myths for that mission statement to hold true. I mean Gaia, Helios, Selene, Themis, Mnemosyne and Eos to name a few Greeks all worked hand in hand with the Gods. Ran and Aegir threw parties for the Asgardians...do you really go to someone's house and eat their food and drink their wine if you think they are evil and just want to kill you?<br /> <br /> I think allying with a titan is pretty much like finding an estranged uncle and hearing their side of things...they are literally family in many cases and if there was no bad blood between the scions and the titan in particular I don't see any reason not to explore this idea further. It would add a lot of nuance to the game in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T00:17:21-07:00","id":912132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/912094-pantheon-creation-with-the-titans-helping#post912094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I Just came up with this really cool idea, We kniw for a fact Scions can create new pantheons,althought there's no mechanics in how to do it just yet,i was thinking that almost all ancinet pantheons had their start with the Titans,the first gods were issues of the titans. I realized,if a band of scions like the sample characters from the first edition were to create a new pantheon,could they strike a deal with the titans to help? (i know <i>all </i>titans were evil in the first edition,but bear with me here). My idea is that the Band could convince a titan to make a connection with their brand new pantheon,one of more mebers of the band would somehow bond with a avatar of titans and they would be connected forever. And they would throw away their relationships with their divine parents and instead be reborn as &quot;scions&quot; of titans. But not like a corrupted scion,they would become flesh and blood of titans,just like any son or daughter of titans would be. so,the same way zeus poseidon and hades and their sisters founded the theoi after being born of cronos and rhea,a modern scion could crteate a new pantheon with the titans help</div> </div> </div> </div>If you scrap the 'All Titans are Evil' thing, this is actually really a sensible way to go about founding a Pantheon. I can possibly see the idea of 'Bonding' with one, but the Band would need to be very careful choosing. Even the Titans that are not evil can be a bit... funny. Selene, Eos, and Ran, for example, are very big into kidnapping (though to be fair to Selene, she only did it once) people through different means. They are entities who are big primordial representations of focused ideas, so keeping one on your side, without your side just becoming 'Raijin's side', or 'Tsensta's side&quot; due to the sheer power and influence of the titan, may be hard.<br /> <br /> But, I can totally see why a Band may want to do this if they are forming a new Pantheon. First and foremost, protection. Having a full fledged Titan working with you gives you a huge degree of protection, which is <i>really</i> needed when founding a Pantheon from my prospective. If one of the Band member's Pantheons have Vengeance as a Virtue, and as you said the Scions throw away their relationships with their divine parents, this little new proto-Pantheon will be facing the wrath of an older, far larger, and far more powerful Pantheon. There are a lot of other <i>issues</i> that arise if a Band wants to create a new Pantheon, on the political level that is (ignoring mechanical issues), that having a Titan (or, like 3) backing your side would really help with. Grab a Justice Titan and I'm sure the entire process of forming a new Pantheon would be far simpler (though, finding a Justice Titan that is willing to break the rules in such a big way would be difficult to say the least).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T10:22:46-07:00","id":912298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/912094-pantheon-creation-with-the-titans-helping?p=912132#post912132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Grab a Justice Titan and I'm sure the entire process of forming a new Pantheon would be far simpler (though, finding a Justice Titan that is willing to break the rules in such a big way would be difficult to say the least).</div> </div> </div> </div>Just make sure the members of the Pantheon-to-be come from backgrounds where their Pantheon of origin doesn't really have any precedent for the &quot;adults&quot; getting pissed at the &quot;kids&quot; doing their own thing and/or make sure that the appropriate &quot;rules&quot; for pantheon creation are followed - castrating fathers (Greeks and Hittites), making sure that parent's aren't able to have sex anymore (Maori and Egyptian), steal their magic (Egyptian again), win a contest/war of succession (Irish). To the victor go the spoils and all. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T11:27:50-07:00","id":912343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/912094-pantheon-creation-with-the-titans-helping?p=912128#post912128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 'All Titans are EVIL' issue of 1st edition was sort of a hard pill to swallow. It made things easier in the sence that they were simpler. Gods good...titans bad...smash titans. But there are so many stories about gods getting along with titans, falling for them and having children with them and working along side them that you have to ignore a lot of myths for that mission statement to hold true. I mean Gaia, Helios, Selene, Themis, Mnemosyne and Eos to name a few Greeks all worked hand in hand with the Gods. Ran and Aegir threw parties for the Asgardians...do you really go to someone's house and eat their food and drink their wine if you think they are evil and just want to kill you?<br /> <br /> I think allying with a titan is pretty much like finding an estranged uncle and hearing their side of things...they are literally family in many cases and if there was no bad blood between the scions and the titan in particular I don't see any reason not to explore this idea further. It would add a lot of nuance to the game in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nuance! i love nuance! I've come up with a way to take this idea further. In the World Blog post,Neall explained ALL creation myths are true no matter how contraditory. And he also said creating a new Creation Myth is actually part of creating a new pantheon. I Remember thinking &quot;wait,How any Band of Scions could create a new Creation Myth now,in 2016?&quot;. And then i realized that may happen by Retroactively Rewriting the World. Basically,in my idea the Scion and their chosen Titan would come up with their creation myth. It'd be like any writer writing their story,and once they are all bound Together in Fate as Brand new pantheon,Their Creation Myth becomes part of the World History. <br /> Example:The Scion talks to a Titan of fire,and they come up with the Myth of the Wold being forged out of gigantic firestorm. After the process is finished,that gigantic firestorm is just as real as Amun creating the Ennead from the Sea,or the Sons of Burr creating the earth from Ymir bones. The scions didnt just become ancient Beings,the were still born on the eighties and their pantheon was still made on 2016,but the story behind the pantheon which is the thing that links them with the titan in Fate's eyes,is just as ancient as the others","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T11:29:11-07:00","id":912345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/912094-pantheon-creation-with-the-titans-helping?p=912132#post912132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you scrap the 'All Titans are Evil' thing, this is actually really a sensible way to go about founding a Pantheon. I can possibly see the idea of 'Bonding' with one, but the Band would need to be very careful choosing. Even the Titans that are not evil can be a bit... funny. Selene, Eos, and Ran, for example, are very big into kidnapping (though to be fair to Selene, she only did it once) people through different means. They are entities who are big primordial representations of focused ideas, so keeping one on your side, without your side just becoming 'Raijin's side', or 'Tsensta's side&quot; due to the sheer power and influence of the titan, may be hard.<br /> <br /> But, I can totally see why a Band may want to do this if they are forming a new Pantheon. First and foremost, protection. Having a full fledged Titan working with you gives you a huge degree of protection, which is <i>really</i> needed when founding a Pantheon from my prospective. If one of the Band member's Pantheons have Vengeance as a Virtue, and as you said the Scions throw away their relationships with their divine parents, this little new proto-Pantheon will be facing the wrath of an older, far larger, and far more powerful Pantheon. There are a lot of other <i>issues</i> that arise if a Band wants to create a new Pantheon, on the political level that is (ignoring mechanical issues), that having a Titan (or, like 3) backing your side would really help with. Grab a Justice Titan and I'm sure the entire process of forming a new Pantheon would be far simpler (though, finding a Justice Titan that is willing to break the rules in such a big way would be difficult to say the least).</div> </div> </div> </div> A Justice titan could literraly make Other's Pantheon's unable to hurt the New One. They could just say it wouldn't be Just,and stop it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T11:33:03-07:00","id":912349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/912094-pantheon-creation-with-the-titans-helping?p=912298#post912298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just make sure the members of the Pantheon-to-be come from backgrounds where their Pantheon of origin doesn't really have any precedent for the &quot;adults&quot; getting pissed at the &quot;kids&quot; doing their own thing and/or make sure that the appropriate &quot;rules&quot; for pantheon creation are followed - castrating fathers (Greeks and Hittites), making sure that parent's aren't able to have sex anymore (Maori and Egyptian), steal their magic (Egyptian again), win a contest/war of succession (Irish). To the victor go the spoils and all.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>i never really understood how the stealing magic bit worked in the scionverse","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T11:56:54-07:00","id":912362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/912094-pantheon-creation-with-the-titans-helping?p=912349#post912349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i never really understood how the stealing magic bit worked in the scionverse</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably some high level Magic stuff that you'd have to make up. Which make sense.... Isis and all....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T12:20:09-07:00","id":912373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/912094-pantheon-creation-with-the-titans-helping?p=912362#post912362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably some high level Magic stuff that you'd have to make up. Which make sense.... Isis and all....</div> </div> </div> </div>she was suuuuuch a bully on that myth","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T13:07:13-07:00","id":912397,"title":"","content":"Do we know if Aten-re was a god or a titan?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T14:58:12-07:00","id":912460,"title":"","content":"Aten? The big solar disk with all the hands that was sort of the first crack at Monotheism? Yeah, he's the Light Titan. I don't really like how he's presented since he single handedly just destroys plot points (Like, I think it mentions he destroyed Helios for one? They were really pushing that 'Only one Light Titan' thing to try to 'deal with' Monotheism) which is too bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T15:23:38-07:00","id":912480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/912094-pantheon-creation-with-the-titans-helping?p=912460#post912460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aten? The big solar disk with all the hands that was sort of the first crack at Monotheism? Yeah, he's the Light Titan. I don't really like how he's presented since he single handedly just destroys plot points (Like, I think it mentions he destroyed Helios for one? They were really pushing that 'Only one Light Titan' thing to try to 'deal with' Monotheism) which is too bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant, Ra sorry,the one with the solar boat","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T15:34:02-07:00","id":912484,"title":"","content":"Ah, no worries. I almost wrote a post about Atum-Ra before catching it was Aten there.<br /> <br /> Ra, Re, Atum-Re, is a tricky figure. He is exceptionally Titan-y in the way I judge them. He is monumentally powerful (note that everything I am about to say here sort of waxes and wanes with the Egyptians since they kicked around for four thousand years and the narratives kept shifting depending on time, city, cult politics, ect) creating the world, and being capable of ending it all if he just shuts his eyes. Additionally, he is somewhat distant, after the rise of the Cult of Isis and her family, Atum-Re sort of gets shuffled out of the main picture, and even before that wasn't doing much interaction with the Pantheon itself short of the solar barge I believe.<br /> <br /> But, then we have the myth of Isis stealing some of his power through his true name which disrupts all of the previous information. From my respective, Ra is a God who is <i>exceptionally close</i> to being a Titan, and possibly has been a Titan in the past. But, by taking his true name, I would say Isis somehow managed to gut Atum-Re of his Titanhood in order to allow her son Horus an easier time in usurping his role as Solar Deity. (I will admit here that when we depict Isis in our games, she tends to be like a Super-Mom, but willing to cut anyone's throat to advance the power of her immediate family. So, the specifies of her character and why she took Ra's power could vary depending on how you depict her)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T15:36:06-07:00","id":912486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/912094-pantheon-creation-with-the-titans-helping?p=912484#post912484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, no worries. I almost wrote a post about Atum-Ra before catching it was Aten there.<br /> <br /> Ra, Re, Atum-Re, is a tricky figure. He is exceptionally Titan-y in the way I judge them. He is monumentally powerful (note that everything I am about to say here sort of waxes and wanes with the Egyptians since they kicked around for four thousand years and the narratives kept shifting depending on time, city, cult politics, ect) creating the world, and being capable of ending it all if he just shuts his eyes. Additionally, he is somewhat distant, after the rise of the Cult of Isis and her family, Atum-Re sort of gets shuffled out of the main picture, and even before that wasn't doing much interaction with the Pantheon itself short of the solar barge I believe.<br /> <br /> But, then we have the myth of Isis stealing some of his power through his true name which disrupts all of the previous information. From my respective, Ra is a God who is <i>exceptionally close</i> to being a Titan, and possibly has been a Titan in the past. But, by taking his true name, I would say Isis somehow managed to gut Atum-Re of his Titanhood in order to allow her son Horus an easier time in usurping his role as Solar Deity. (I will admit here that when we depict Isis in our games, she tends to be like a Super-Mom, but willing to cut anyone's throat to advance the power of her immediate family. So, the specifies of her character and why she took Ra's power could vary depending on how you depict her)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats really cool,I hope the Netherlands on the new scion edition will be like that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T11:02:47-07:00","id":913517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/912094-pantheon-creation-with-the-titans-helping#post912094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I Just came up with this really cool idea, We kniw for a fact Scions can create new pantheons,althought there's no mechanics in how to do it just yet,i was thinking that almost all ancinet pantheons had their start with the Titans,the first gods were issues of the titans. I realized,if a band of scions like the sample characters from the first edition were to create a new pantheon,could they strike a deal with the titans to help? (i know <i>all </i>titans were evil in the first edition,but bear with me here). My idea is that the Band could convince a titan to make a connection with their brand new pantheon,one of more mebers of the band would somehow bond with a avatar of titans and they would be connected forever. And they would throw away their relationships with their divine parents and instead be reborn as &quot;scions&quot; of titans. But not like a corrupted scion,they would become flesh and blood of titans,just like any son or daughter of titans would be. so,the same way zeus poseidon and hades and their sisters founded the theoi after being born of cronos and rhea,a modern scion could crteate a new pantheon with the titans help</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I wouldn't strictly call the Titans evil, they're just more primal than the Gods, which is actually saying quite a lot.<br /> <br /> First edition even suggests that Gaia, the prime avatar of Terra, would have actually been willing to go back to Tartarus if Zeus simply recognized her children as equals. Of course, these are the Greeks, and that sure as hell wasn't going to happen.<br /> <br /> <br /> And Prometheus was a Titan who represented the creative power of fire. He simply wasn't concerned about the applications of what he was creating, which made him come across as being a bit careless with his designs.<br /> <br /> So yeah, there are possible Titans who may assist the Scions in creating new pantheons. The question is how the current pantheons would react to such an alliance. Remember what happened to the Atlanteans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-13-2016, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T11:56:29-07:00","id":913555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/912094-pantheon-creation-with-the-titans-helping?p=913517#post913517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I wouldn't strictly call the Titans evil, they're just more primal than the Gods, which is actually saying quite a lot.<br /> <br /> First edition even suggests that Gaia, the prime avatar of Terra, would have actually been willing to go back to Tartarus if Zeus simply recognized her children as equals. Of course, these are the Greeks, and that sure as hell wasn't going to happen.<br /> <br /> <br /> And Prometheus was a Titan who represented the creative power of fire. He simply wasn't concerned about the applications of what he was creating, which made him come across as being a bit careless with his designs.<br /> <br /> So yeah, there are possible Titans who may assist the Scions in creating new pantheons. The question is how the current pantheons would react to such an alliance. Remember what happened to the Atlanteans?</div> </div> </div> </div>i feel like if the new Pantheon to be would approach the Titan from a place of humbleness,and politely ask the titan to help,and explain to the titan what they could gain from the deal,no trickery,no,backstabiing, just a honest deal. it would work fine. but i <i>am </i>conting on 2e titans being a bit more resonable","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T12:13:15-07:00","id":913569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/912094-pantheon-creation-with-the-titans-helping?p=913517#post913517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Prometheus was a Titan who represented the creative power of fire. He simply wasn't concerned about the applications of what he was creating, which made him come across as being a bit careless with his designs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh a soapbox for be to throw rocks at Prometheus, awesome. Sorry if this is a bit off topic, but I want to yell about Prometheus for a moment.<br /> <br /> Prometheus has the greatest PR of any Titan. People always talk about Prometheus being this martyr for the humans going against the will of Heaven modernly, which is a really lovely idea (which Prometheus in a Scion game could <i>really</i> monopolize on to get Scions to work for him) but I feel misses the core point of mortals being irelevent to the divine in Greek Mythology, and slightly misunderstands the order of events with Prometheus. So, I've got this slightly different way to present Prometheus trying to be more in line with the characters. <br /> <br /> So, the Titanomachy kicks off, and the Titans that stay neutral (Oceanus), or side with the upstart children of Cronus (Hecate, also possibly Helios, Selene, and Eos) are, in the end, not thrown into Tatarus (or otherwise imprisoned) by Zeus. For some reason, Prometheus and Epimetheus (who is Afterthought or Hindsight) are not imprisoned alongside their brother Atlas, and father Iapetus. So, thereby we can conclude Prometheus was either neutral or sided with the Gods (I think this is even outright stated in Prometheus Bound).<br /> <br /> Now, from here, there are two important parts of information that need to be remembered. First, Prometheus isn't a Titan of creative fire, or the like, despite him being presented so modernly. Prometheus is the primordial force of Forethought (its his name), and this is important to remember. Just like Oceanus is the rim-ocean, Erebus is darkness, and Nix is night, Prometheus is the literal manifestation of Forethought. Secondly, mortals are presented as being ultimately irelevent to the Divine. We are like mayflies to them (I swear this is a line in the Illiad or something, but I have never been able to find it. So I am slightly unsure.) and spectacularly irelevent unless they've decided they fancy us. So, with these two bits of information we can glean that Prometheus has thought out every single thing he is going to be doing and the consequences of his actions as he is the literal embodiment of Forethought. Secondly, that he likely doesn't care much for mortals.<br /> <br /> But, why would Prometheus preform The Trick at Mecone (the trick of getting Zeus to select the worse sort of sacrifices) then? We are never directly told in Hesiod's Theogony. So, we need to infer. Since Mortals are silly little creatures who have mayfly lives, he probably isn't doing this to help them. Prometheus' brother, father, and mother were all imprisoned by Zeus after the war, but Prometheus sided with Zeus. However, Atlas is being singled out, and punished in a very specific way (forced to hold the sky aloft) which in its uniqueness makes a good source of Prometheus' ire.<br /> <br /> So, Prometheus then tricks Zeus into accepting the worse sacrifice from mortals. Grecian sacrifice was fire sacrifice where you burned the offerings, mortals had a summit with Zeus at a place called Mecone where they wanted him to specify the sort of sacrifices he wanted. Prometheus killed an ox, and divided its body up into two piles. He took all of the ox's meat, fat, and otherly tasty bits the Gods and Humans both wanted, and shoved them into the ox's stomach. He then took all of the bones, and wrapped them up in the cow's hide.<br /> <br /> Zeus, looking at these two piles, is tricked by Prometheus into accepting the bundle which looks more pleasing, and resigning the Pantheon to sacrifices of bones and other waste from butchery while those blasted mortals get the tasty bits. (Hesiod presents this as Zeus being benevolent to the mortals, but this doesn't make sense if you realize what happens next) So, Zeus is mad, and takes fire away from humanity in punishment. (They can't preform the sacrifices without the fire, so Zeus is feeling a bit better about himself. Showed those mortals. But, this bit also sort of disproves that Zeus was being benevolent in picking the worse bundle since he instantly punished the mortals for it)<br /> <br /> Now, Prometheus looks at this and sees his trick is now ultimately pointless. The humans can't snub the Theoi without fire, all his trickery has been for nothing. Since mortals are irelevent little gnats, he's probably not doing this directly for their sake as well. So, he goes and grabs a fennel stalk, puts an ember from Hestia's hearth in it, and legs it down the mountain. He gives it to humanity, and woo, they have fire back, everyone's nice and warm, they can contact the divine through sacrifices, all is nice.<br /> <br /> Except Zeus is double pissed. Prometheus keeps showing off that Zeus is not omniscient despite him insisting that he is. So, Kratos and Ba (Strength and Force, two Titans who serve as Zeus bodyguards) snatch up Prometheus, and Hephaestus binds him to the mountain where an eagle rips out his liver and eats it every day. Now, keep in mind, as Forethought, Prometheus probably knew this would happen. Humanity, and Epimetheus both get punished as well for Prometheus' crime because, you know, Zeus, by the creation of Pandora. Bad stuff happens, humanity is thrown into chaos, all the evils of the world unleashed. Now, remember, Prometheus is Forethought, and probably knew that this would have happened.<br /> <br /> Then, Prometheus (in Prometheus Bound) actually directly showcases his capacity as Forethought. He lets it slip that he knows the identity of The Son of Zeus who is fated to overthrow him. Zeus, who was pretty sure he nipped this curse from Gaia in the bud when he ate his first wife Metis, loses it. He sends everyone to go try to get this information out of Prometheus, but Prometheus ignores it.<br /> <br /> And then, one day, Hercules arrives and frees Prometheus. Prometheus vanishes from the mythic record, and is never seen or heard from again. But, he <i>does not</i> like Zeus, and knows who The Son of Zeus will be / is. So, as the literal embodiment of Forethought, he likely is just hiding out, and biding his time.<br /> <br /> But yeah, round about way of saying Prometheus probably doesn't like humans, just really doesn't like Zeus. Ajax knows more about the Theoi than I do, but I think the characterization is pretty solid for this presentation of Prometheus. Prometheus as Forethought and not some fire Titan I find to be far more interesting as a story thread.<br /> <br /> ... I'll get off my soapbox now, sorry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/912094-pantheon-creation-with-the-titans-helping?p=913517#post913517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yeah, there are possible Titans who may assist the Scions in creating new pantheons. The question is how the current pantheons would react to such an alliance. Remember what happened to the Atlanteans?</div> </div> </div> </div>Was that what happened to the Atlanteans in RAW? That's weird. Most of the Pantheons have Titan allies, but, you know. RAW. The Theoi have Oceanus, Helios, Hecate, Eos, Selene, Nix, Ba, Kratos, and all the other children of Nix. The Tuatha would have Danu (should be a Titan, not a Goddess), and have been allied with Lir in the past until Bobd Derg revealed that he is The Worst King and shouldn't be allowed to make political decisions. The Netjer have Ma'at, the Aesir have Ran (and probably don't have issues with Mani and Sol, but they're otherwise occupied by Hadi and Skoll), the Kami have Izanagi (who like Danu should be a Titan) and the like. Pantheons having Titan allies is sort of normal. But, you're right Nyrufa, RAW didn't actually point this out. <br /> <br /> Which I find is too bad. I like allied Titans as a way to showcase why Titans are scary without being a direct threat to a Band. I think the Band meeting Lir after curing his children of their curse is probably one of my favorite moments of a game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T12:29:34-07:00","id":913579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/912094-pantheon-creation-with-the-titans-helping?p=913569#post913569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh a soapbox for be to throw rocks at Prometheus, awesome. Sorry if this is a bit off topic, but I want to yell about Prometheus for a moment.<br /> <br /> Prometheus has the greatest PR of any Titan. People always talk about Prometheus being this martyr for the humans going against the will of Heaven modernly, which is a really lovely idea (which Prometheus in a Scion game could <i>really</i> monopolize on to get Scions to work for him) but I feel misses the core point of mortals being irelevent to the divine in Greek Mythology, and slightly misunderstands the order of events with Prometheus. So, I've got this slightly different way to present Prometheus trying to be more in line with the characters.<br /> <br /> So, the Titanomachy kicks off, and the Titans that stay neutral (Oceanus), or side with the upstart children of Cronus (Hecate, also possibly Helios, Selene, and Eos) are, in the end, not thrown into Tatarus (or otherwise imprisoned) by Zeus. For some reason, Prometheus and Epimetheus (who is Afterthought or Hindsight) are not imprisoned alongside their brother Atlas, and father Iapetus. So, thereby we can conclude Prometheus was either neutral or sided with the Gods (I think this is even outright stated in Prometheus Bound).<br /> <br /> Now, from here, there are two important parts of information that need to be remembered. First, Prometheus isn't a Titan of creative fire, or the like, despite him being presented so modernly. Prometheus is the primordial force of Forethought (its his name), and this is important to remember. Just like Oceanus is the rim-ocean, Erebus is darkness, and Nix is night, Prometheus is the literal manifestation of Forethought. Secondly, mortals are presented as being ultimately irelevent to the Divine. We are like mayflies to them (I swear this is a line in the Illiad or something, but I have never been able to find it. So I am slightly unsure.) and spectacularly irelevent unless they've decided they fancy us. So, with these two bits of information we can glean that Prometheus has thought out every single thing he is going to be doing and the consequences of his actions as he is the literal embodiment of Forethought. Secondly, that he likely doesn't care much for mortals.<br /> <br /> But, why would Prometheus preform The Trick at Mecone (the trick of getting Zeus to select the worse sort of sacrifices) then? We are never directly told in Hesiod's Theogony. So, we need to infer. Since Mortals are silly little creatures who have mayfly lives, he probably isn't doing this to help them. Prometheus' brother, father, and mother were all imprisoned by Zeus after the war, but Prometheus sided with Zeus. However, Atlas is being singled out, and punished in a very specific way (forced to hold the sky aloft) which in its uniqueness makes a good source of Prometheus' ire.<br /> <br /> So, Prometheus then tricks Zeus into accepting the worse sacrifice from mortals. Grecian sacrifice was fire sacrifice where you burned the offerings, mortals had a summit with Zeus at a place called Mecone where they wanted him to specify the sort of sacrifices he wanted. Prometheus killed an ox, and divided its body up into two piles. He took all of the ox's meat, fat, and otherly tasty bits the Gods and Humans both wanted, and shoved them into the ox's stomach. He then took all of the bones, and wrapped them up in the cow's hide.<br /> <br /> Zeus, looking at these two piles, is tricked by Prometheus into accepting the bundle which looks more pleasing, and resigning the Pantheon to sacrifices of bones and other waste from butchery while those blasted mortals get the tasty bits. (Hesiod presents this as Zeus being benevolent to the mortals, but this doesn't make sense if you realize what happens next) So, Zeus is mad, and takes fire away from humanity in punishment. (They can't preform the sacrifices without the fire, so Zeus is feeling a bit better about himself. Showed those mortals. But, this bit also sort of disproves that Zeus was being benevolent in picking the worse bundle since he instantly punished the mortals for it)<br /> <br /> Now, Prometheus looks at this and sees his trick is now ultimately pointless. The humans can't snub the Theoi without fire, all his trickery has been for nothing. Since mortals are irelevent little gnats, he's probably not doing this directly for their sake as well. So, he goes and grabs a fennel stalk, puts an ember from Hestia's hearth in it, and legs it down the mountain. He gives it to humanity, and woo, they have fire back, everyone's nice and warm, they can contact the divine through sacrifices, all is nice.<br /> <br /> Except Zeus is double pissed. Prometheus keeps showing off that Zeus is not omniscient despite him insisting that he is. So, Kratos and Ba (Strength and Force, two Titans who serve as Zeus bodyguards) snatch up Prometheus, and Hephaestus binds him to the mountain where an eagle rips out his liver and eats it every day. Now, keep in mind, as Forethought, Prometheus probably knew this would happen. Humanity, and Epimetheus both get punished as well for Prometheus' crime because, you know, Zeus, by the creation of Pandora. Bad stuff happens, humanity is thrown into chaos, all the evils of the world unleashed. Now, remember, Prometheus is Forethought, and probably knew that this would have happened.<br /> <br /> Then, Prometheus (in Prometheus Bound) actually directly showcases his capacity as Forethought. He lets it slip that he knows the identity of The Son of Zeus who is fated to overthrow him. Zeus, who was pretty sure he nipped this curse from Gaia in the bud when he ate his first wife Metis, loses it. He sends everyone to go try to get this information out of Prometheus, but Prometheus ignores it.<br /> <br /> And then, one day, Hercules arrives and frees Prometheus. Prometheus vanishes from the mythic record, and is never seen or heard from again. But, he <i>does not</i> like Zeus, and knows who The Son of Zeus will be / is. So, as the literal embodiment of Forethought, he likely is just hiding out, and biding his time.<br /> <br /> But yeah, round about way of saying Prometheus probably doesn't like humans, just really doesn't like Zeus. Ajax knows more about the Theoi than I do, but I think the characterization is pretty solid for this presentation of Prometheus. Prometheus as Forethought and not some fire Titan I find to be far more interesting as a story thread.<br /> <br /> ... I'll get off my soapbox now, sorry.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Was that what happened to the Atlanteans in RAW? That's weird. Most of the Pantheons have Titan allies, but, you know. RAW. The Theoi have Oceanus, Helios, Hecate, Eos, Selene, Nix, Ba, Kratos, and all the other children of Nix. The Tuatha would have Danu (should be a Titan, not a Goddess), and have been allied with Lir in the past until Bobd Derg revealed that he is The Worst King and shouldn't be allowed to make political decisions. The Netjer have Ma'at, the Aesir have Ran (and probably don't have issues with Mani and Sol, but they're otherwise occupied by Hadi and Skoll), the Kami have Izanagi (who like Danu should be a Titan) and the like. Pantheons having Titan allies is sort of normal. But, you're right Nyrufa, RAW didn't actually point this out.<br /> <br /> Which I find is too bad. I like allied Titans as a way to showcase why Titans are scary without being a direct threat to a Band. I think the Band meeting Lir after curing his children of their curse is probably one of my favorite moments of a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>you could argue if prometheus become part of the new pantheon,one of the new pantheons Virtues could be Forethought","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T13:43:14-07:00","id":913633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/912094-pantheon-creation-with-the-titans-helping?p=913579#post913579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you could argue if prometheus become part of the new pantheon,one of the new pantheons Virtues could be Forethought</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Prometheus could make a really good Titan for helping a new Pantheon. In fact, in my games Prometheus is constantly waiting in the wings for The Son of Zeus. Unsure if that would really count as forming a 'New' Pantheon in as much as it's overthrowing a previous, but that's 100% what Prometheus gets up to in mine. Just biding his time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T16:17:53-07:00","id":913713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/912094-pantheon-creation-with-the-titans-helping?p=913569#post913569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Was that what happened to the Atlanteans in RAW? That's weird. Most of the Pantheons have Titan allies, but, you know. RAW. The Theoi have Oceanus, Helios, Hecate, Eos, Selene, Nix, Ba, Kratos, and all the other children of Nix. The Tuatha would have Danu (should be a Titan, not a Goddess), and have been allied with Lir in the past until Bobd Derg revealed that he is The Worst King and shouldn't be allowed to make political decisions. The Netjer have Ma'at, the Aesir have Ran (and probably don't have issues with Mani and Sol, but they're otherwise occupied by Hadi and Skoll), the Kami have Izanagi (who like Danu should be a Titan) and the like. Pantheons having Titan allies is sort of normal. But, you're right Nyrufa, RAW didn't actually point this out.<br /> <br /> Which I find is too bad. I like allied Titans as a way to showcase why Titans are scary without being a direct threat to a Band. I think the Band meeting Lir after curing his children of their curse is probably one of my favorite moments of a game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, as I remember it from the book, the Atlanteans pantheon began to form open alliances with the Titans and encourage Titan worship. At the time, the Atlanteans were perhaps the most advanced civilization, so the Gods took offense to that and wiped them out. And this wasn't some simple war. Every pantheon in the world joined hands, sang Kum Ba Yah, and performed mass genocide of the Atlantean culture. All because they decided to find something else to worship. One of the Egyptian gods managed to save a scrap of their history because that's what his role in the pantheon was. A lore master, or something of that nature.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for your idea on Prometheus, I think you're confusing Forethought with Precognition. Regardless, whatever plan he had to discredit Zeus seems to have worked over time. Given Zeus' reputation in the present day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-13-2016, 07:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T16:38:31-07:00","id":913724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/912094-pantheon-creation-with-the-titans-helping?p=913569#post913569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But yeah, round about way of saying Prometheus probably doesn't like humans, just really doesn't like Zeus. Ajax knows more about the Theoi than I do, but I think the characterization is pretty solid for this presentation of Prometheus. Prometheus as Forethought and not some fire Titan I find to be far more interesting as a story thread.<br /> <br /> ... I'll get off my soapbox now, sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do? I'm not sure that is the case... But I can see your points about Prometheus<br /> <br /> Given all you said, there are also some stories where Prometheus is the creator of humanity and the instigator of their Golden Age... but that could just add complexity to the whole thing. How far ahead is he seeing, exactly?<br /> <br /> I also wonder if his and his brother's having been spared Tartarus might have been some intervention from auntie Metis, as her &quot;sphere&quot; seems to intersect strongly with theirs. They would definitely all be Titans (or &quot;Titanides&quot;) who would HAVE to see the writing on the wall about the triumph of the Gods in the Titanomachy. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T17:10:08-07:00","id":913735,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/912094-pantheon-creation-with-the-titans-helping?p=913713#post913713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for your idea on Prometheus, I think you're confusing Forethought with Precognition. Regardless, whatever plan he had to discredit Zeus seems to have worked over time. Given Zeus' reputation in the present day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I didn't explain that bit very well. What I mean isn't that Prometheus has advanced knowledge of what will be, but as he is primordial forethought, he (in the nature of what he is) have thought out his actions. It's not that he knows what will happen, but that when Prometheus sits down and thinks he can work out what will happen. It's one of those weird places where sufficiently high enough Epic Intelligence can start looking <i>very</i> similar to Prophecy. Even though it isn't supported in RAW, Prometheus is pretty much a Titan of Epic Intelligence.<br /> <br /> So, it wouldn't be that Prometheus has foreknowledge, but he has thought everything out to the extent that a Titan of Forethought would be able to. Just like how Oceanus is better at using Water than Poseidon, Prometheus (in his specific area of Forethought, probably not things like invention) can out Forethink people like Thoth. Essentially, Prometheus could 'plan' at a Titanic level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/912094-pantheon-creation-with-the-titans-helping?p=913724#post913724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do? I'm not sure that is the case... But I can see your points about Prometheus.<br /> <br /> Given all you said, there are also some stories where Prometheus is the creator of humanity and the instigator of their Golden Age... but that could just add complexity to the whole thing. How far ahead is he seeing, exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh man, yeah, that's sort of a weird kettle of fish with the theory. I've not heard of the Golden Age bit before, but I guess that would have taken place back with Cronus? The creator of humanity bit is really tricky due to the different 'Eras' of humanity in Greek thought. If I remember correctly, when Prometheus makes humans, it's on the behest of Zeus, which means it is Silver, Bronze, Heroic, or Iron. It couldn't be Iron, or Heroic however since Prometheus is freed by Heracles who is from the Heroic Age. (unless he created the first generation and then got imprisoned) Bronze doesn't work either since Zeus is directly credited as their creator. I think Silver may be the best however, since they end up getting destroyed by Zeus for impiety (which Prometheus constantly showing off that Zeus isn't omniscient could have caused) which could work.<br /> <br /> But, since he is also making all of the animals, it couldn't be the Silver Age humans since Zeus specifically targeted the humans from that age. Making the animals is unnessessary unless they have all died. (since animals and humans did exist during Cronus Golden Age. At least, I am sure Humans did exist) So, this fits in better with it happening chronologically after Zeus has to flood the planet to save Gaia from Helios son flying the sun too close to the earth. Since everyone and everything perished in the flood (IIRC), then Prometheus making both humans and animals works a bit better. But, it isn't clear what age this happened in except it can't be the Golden Age.<br /> <br /> So... yeah, my answer to that is I have no idea how it could work mostly because the Ages of Man are really complicated, and the creation of the animals throws it all off. If you want to fiddle slightly and add in a delay of time between the creation of humans and the sacrifice trick, the theory could work nicely. If Prometheus created one age, which then gets destroyed by Zeus in one of the ways he does it, he may be infuriated by this and that could be why he is acting against Zeus.<br /> <br /> In that slight twisting of the narrative, Prometheus liked <i>his</i> humans. <i>His</i> humans were interesting creatures. But then Zeus killed them all, so he spoiled the next batch too. When he returns and sees the lower ages of Humanity, he would then just be disappointed in almost 'failed creations'.<br /> <br /> Edit: Forgot the second bit. In my head, Prometheus 'worked out' up to Heracles saving him. He knew that, in the end, he would 'get away' with it all, even being saved by one of Zeus' own sons. When he starts 'watching' humanity, especially modern humanity, I can see him being surprised that his whole ploy resulted in him being immortalized as a pro-human entity, and taking advantage of it. Especially if The Son of Zeus is born and he can swing by going, &quot;Hey! It's Prometheus! I'm a benevolent entity! Let's have a conversation about your father.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/912094-pantheon-creation-with-the-titans-helping?p=913724#post913724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also wonder if his and his brother's having been spared Tartarus might have been some intervention from auntie Metis, as her &quot;sphere&quot; seems to intersect strongly with theirs. They would definitely all be Titans (or &quot;Titanides&quot;) who would HAVE to see the writing on the wall about the triumph of the Gods in the Titanomachy.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a good way to explain it! Hecate, and Nix both see the writing on the wall in the Theogony, but Prometheus, Epimetheus, and Metis go unexplained. It would make total sense that they would be able to see that Cronus was going to lose this one due to the nature of what they are. There is also something that could be done with Prometheus knowing the identity of The Son of Zeus who is supposed to be Metis' son.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 06-13-2016, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3